@startuml fix-implementer
title FixImplementer — one log finding, keyed by fingerprint\nSame shape as LinearImplementer, plus the right to refuse

scale 0.8
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam StateBorderColor Black
skinparam StateFontColor Black
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor White
skinparam NoteBorderColor Black
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BackgroundColor<<Package>> LightBlue
    BackgroundColor<<Final>> LightGreen
    BackgroundColor<<Error>> LightCoral
}

state "WORKING" as working <<Package>> {

    state "fi_pending" as Pending
        Pending: - instance exists, no run dispatched
        Pending: - fingerprint, repo, service, environment

    state "fi_implementing" as Implementing
        Implementing: - FixImplementer running
        Implementing: - validates the finding BEFORE editing
        Implementing: - dispatched again if no run is alive

    state "fi_verifying" as Verifying
        Verifying: - FixVerifier: no run yet, nothing claimed verified
        Verifying: - releases the draft PR: draft -> ready for review

    state "fi_needs_human" as NeedsHuman <<Error>>
        NeedsHuman: - OPEN, not final
        NeedsHuman: - the fix run failed

    state "fi_discarded" as Discarded <<Final>>
        Discarded: - no PR: false_positive, unreproducible,
        Discarded:   operational_issue, outside_repo,
        Discarded:   already_fixed, unsafe_to_change,
        Discarded:   insufficient_evidence

    state "fi_dismissed" as Dismissed <<Final>>
        Dismissed: - a person stopped it instead of retrying
}

state "RELEASED — PrMaintainer maintains the PR" as released <<Package>> {

    state "fi_waiting_pr" as WaitingPr
        WaitingPr: - PR ready for review
        WaitingPr: - checked hourly until merged or closed

    state "fi_done" as Done <<Final>>
        Done: - PR merged

    state "fi_abandoned" as Abandoned <<Final>>
        Abandoned: - PR closed without merging
}

[*] -r-> Pending: OnFindingReported

Pending -r-> Implementing: handleStateFiPending\nOnPeriodicCheck(dispatch owed)\nOnSystemRecovery(dispatch owed)
Implementing -r-> Verifying: OnSandboxRunSucceeded(draft PR opened)
Implementing -d-> Discarded: OnSandboxRunSucceeded(no PR, reason)
Implementing -[#Red]-> NeedsHuman: OnSandboxRunFailed\nOnPeriodicCheck(run lost)\nOnSystemRecovery(run lost)

NeedsHuman -u-> Implementing: OnOperatorRetry
NeedsHuman -d-> Dismissed: OnOperatorDismiss

Verifying ---> WaitingPr: OnPeriodicCheck(draft released)
working -r-> Done: OnPrMerged
working -d-> Abandoned: OnPrClosed
WaitingPr -d-> Done: OnPeriodicCheck(PR merged)
WaitingPr -d-> Abandoned: OnPeriodicCheck(PR closed)

Done -d-> [*]
Abandoned -d-> [*]
Discarded -d-> [*]
Dismissed -d-> [*]

note bottom of Discarded
  Linear has no equivalent: refusing a human's request
  means asking the human (li_needs_human). Here refusing
  is a legitimate outcome, because a machine found the work.
end note

note bottom of Verifying
  Until FixVerifier exists, releasing the draft is all this state does.
  Nothing is recorded as verified: a green that proved nothing is worse
  than no green.
end note

@enduml
